# These files are inputs to, or output of, a build that runs on both Windows (locally)
# and Linux (CI). git's autocrlf would hand Windows a CRLF working copy and Linux an LF
# one; because site/assets/* are include_str!'d straight into the generated page, the
# two platforms would then render byte-different HTML and the CI sync check could never
# pass on both. Pinning LF everywhere makes the render reproducible across platforms.
index.html      text eol=lf
site/assets/*   text eol=lf
site/src/*.rs   text eol=lf
